## Vercel Speed Insights Installation and Configuration

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this React + Vite project.

### Changes Made:

#### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 using npm
- Added to dependencies in `package.json`
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new dependency and its 181 transitive dependencies

#### 2. Code Configuration
Modified `src/App.jsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react';`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component alongside the existing `<Analytics />` component
- Placed within the `<AuthProvider>` wrapper to ensure proper context access
- Follows the same pattern as the existing Vercel Analytics integration

### Implementation Details:

**Framework Detection:**
- Identified React 19.2.8 with Vite 8.3.0
- Used npm as the package manager (detected via package-lock.json)

**Installation Method:**
- Fetched latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
- Followed React-specific integration instructions from the official Vercel docs

**Verification:**
- ✓ Build completed successfully (1.85s)
- ✓ Linter ran without new errors (only pre-existing warnings)
- ✓ No breaking changes introduced
- ✓ Lock file properly updated

### Next Steps:

After deployment to Vercel:
1. Speed Insights will automatically start collecting performance metrics
2. Data will be available in the Vercel dashboard under "Speed Insights"
3. Metrics become available after several days of visitor activity
4. The tracking script deploys automatically at `/_vercel/speed-insights/*`

### Files Modified:
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `src/App.jsx` - Added SpeedInsights component import and usage
